A||||4||VISCERAL||Machining request or a search for steering rack bushings!!!!!
Z||000000||VISCERAL||07-22-99||09:06 PM||||Some of you guys must be experiencing a noise in the front end when you hit a bump. It is kind of a metal klanking sound(please no more noise jokes) that really cheapens the feel of your car. It is in my opinion that it is the steering rack bushing on the passenger side of the rack that has worn out and that it lets the rack rattle around on bumpy surfaces.<br>Who makes our steering rack? <br>The dealerships are out of these bushings to correct it. <br>Can anyone machine out some bronze bushings for a fair price compared to the $275-$325 that the fiero store charges for a new rack.<br>I would rather replace mine for under...let's say $20. I think we could all use one of these, especially the high milers out there. Your rack must be driving you crazy! Can anyone help? 
Z||000001||PaUL||07-22-99||09:11 PM||||I dont know if this is the same noise you are experiencing but I found that alot of the clanking noises from the front were coming from the jack bouncing around. I tightened it down but it still moved around so I inserted pieces of a cutup rubber mudflap in the spaces between the jack and bracket. This got rid of most of the noise. 
Z||000002||ezsurf||07-22-99||09:45 PM||||Visceral,<br>I've been test driving my car around the yard since my rebuild, I have noticed a metal clanking sound.  I have not yet been able to identify it.  It sounds like it is coming from the back of the car, but I will definately check the steering rack.  It's a light clanking sound, it almost has a ring to it.  The emergency jack is not in the car, so that ain't the problem.  I would really like to know what it is.
Z||000003||VISCERAL||07-22-99||10:23 PM||||I'll install some kind of rubber "protection" <br>device near my jack and we'll see what happens. Let you know tomorrow.
Z||000004||VISCERAL||07-23-99||09:18 AM||||Talked to ED PARKS of the Fiero Factory and he said check the coolant tubes-sometimes they are too close to the chassis, and also to check the shock mounts for play.<br>He also said to checkout:<br>CRISWELL CHEVY in Maryland at 1-888-466-9101 <br>they could possibly do a nationwide search for any parts you ned and if your some kinda of club member they'll give you a jobbers price. I have a feeling its one of the coolant tubes because I tried grabbing the toe rod arms and they really wouldn't wiggle in any way so...<br>its not the jack...we'll see
